# Docs: https://trivy.dev/docs/latest/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
# Reviewed Trivy exceptions. Trivy loads this file by default, so it applies to every
# Trivy run from the repository root (`check:scan`, `check:vuln`, and the image gates)
# unless a run passes another `--ignorefile`, as the unfiltered evidence scan in
# scripts/scan_deployed.py does.
# Every entry states why the finding does not apply here — an unexplained id is
# technical debt, and a check silenced without a reason is worse than no check.

# DS-0026 "Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile".
# The deployment target is Cloud Run, which ignores Docker HEALTHCHECK and
# drives health from startup_probe/liveness_probe in infra/cloud_run.tf — both
# already probe /health. Duplicating that policy as dead image metadata would
# create two health contracts while adding no runtime coverage.
DS-0026
